('46918bdd-3210-56d7-9996-1ee1733506d8','ba9fa44b-3021-57c6-b0d3-016073b07be8',1,'adverb','A1','S1','W1',null,'[{"phrase":"more and more","register":null,"definition_en":"used to say that a quality , situation etc gradually increases","translation":"قبلاً می گفتند که یک کیفیت، وضعیت و غیره به تدریج افزایش می یابد","example":"More and more, we are finding that people want to continue working beyond 60.","example_translation":"بیشتر و بیشتر متوجه می شویم که مردم می خواهند بیش از 60 سال به کار خود ادامه دهند.","example_audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001534922.mp3"},{"phrase":"more or less","register":null,"definition_en":"almost","translation":"تقریبا","example":"a place where the ground was more or less flat","example_translation":"جایی که زمین کم و بیش صاف بود","example_audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001534927.mp3"},{"phrase":"once more","register":null,"definition_en":"again, and often for the last time","translation":"دوباره، و اغلب برای آخرین بار","example":"May I thank you all once more for making this occasion such a big success.","example_translation":"ممکن است من یک بار دیگر از همه شما تشکر کنم که این مناسبت را به چنین موفقیت بزرگی تبدیل کردید.","example_audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001534930.mp3"},{"phrase":"not anymore","register":null,"definition_en":"used when something used to happen or be true in the past but does not happen or is not true now","translation":"زمانی استفاده می‌شود که در گذشته اتفاقی می‌افتاد یا درست بود، اما اتفاق نمی‌افتد یا اکنون درست نیست","example":"Nick doesn’t live here anymore.","example_translation":"نیک دیگر اینجا زندگی نمی کند.","example_audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000942680.mp3"},{"phrase":"be more something than something","register":null,"definition_en":"to be one thing rather than another","translation":"یک چیز بودن به جای چیز دیگر","example":"It was more a worry than a pleasure.","example_translation":"این بیشتر یک نگرانی بود تا لذت.","example_audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001821232.mp3"},{"phrase":"more than a little","register":"formal","definition_en":"fairly","translation":"منصفانه","example":"The lectures were more than a little disappointing.","example_translation":"سخنرانی ها بیشتر از کمی ناامید کننده بود.","example_audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001755034.mp3"}]'::jsonb),
('2fc8ee31-e337-5901-b649-565d96d9ff65','ba9fa44b-3021-57c6-b0d3-016073b07be8',2,'determiner','A1','S1','W1','[ comparative of ‘many’ and ‘much’ ]','[{"phrase":"more and more","register":null,"definition_en":"used to say that a quality , situation etc gradually increases","translation":"قبلاً می گفتند که یک کیفیت، وضعیت و غیره به تدریج افزایش می یابد","example":"More and more, we are finding that people want to continue working beyond 60.","example_translation":"بیشتر و بیشتر متوجه می شویم که مردم می خواهند بیش از 60 سال به کار خود ادامه دهند.","example_audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001534922.mp3"},{"phrase":"be more of something than something","register":null,"definition_en":"to be one thing rather than another","translation":"یک چیز بودن به جای چیز دیگر","example":"It was more of a holiday than a training exercise.","example_translation":"این بیشتر یک تعطیلات بود تا تمرین.","example_audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001534973.mp3"},{"phrase":"no more than","register":null,"definition_en":"used to emphasize that someone or something does not have a particular quality or would not do something","translation":"برای تأکید بر اینکه کسی یا چیزی کیفیت خاصی ندارد یا کاری را انجام نمی دهد استفاده می شود","example":"He’s no more fit to be a priest than I am!","example_translation":"او بیشتر از من شایسته کشیش شدن نیست!","example_audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000209662.mp3"},{"phrase":"no more something","register":null,"definition_en":"used to say that something will or should no longer happen","translation":"می گفت که چیزی دیگر اتفاق خواهد افتاد یا نباید اتفاق بیفتد","example":"No more dreary winters – we’re moving to Florida.","example_translation":"دیگر خبری از زمستان های دلگیر نیست - ما به فلوریدا نقل مکان می کنیم.","example_audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001821265.mp3"}]'::jsonb),
('bfc0e9b8-c982-569f-97b5-5aad8b6e54af','27a3d318-76fe-585f-be97-3d719fbe1416',1,'adverb','A1','S1','W1',null,'[]'::jsonb),
('c3118e09-5eb9-55c9-909d-a859579113f6','27a3d318-76fe-585f-be97-3d719fbe1416',2,'determiner','A1','S1','W1','[ the superlative of ‘many’ and ‘much’ ]','[{"phrase":"for the most part","register":null,"definition_en":"used to say that something is generally true but not completely true","translation":"معمولاً می‌گفتند چیزی به طور کلی درست است اما کاملاً درست نیست","example":"For the most part, people seemed pretty friendly.","example_translation":"در بیشتر موارد، مردم بسیار دوستانه به نظر می رسیدند.","example_audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000210899.mp3"}]'::jsonb),
('63573673-c1e8-5f42-bb3f-c6f08f48bea4','27a3d318-76fe-585f-be97-3d719fbe1416',3,'suffix','A1',null,null,'[ in adjectives ]','[]'::jsonb),
('2244fcb1-5206-5ffe-a4a7-be4895dbab8c','3b1d659c-6230-5724-8163-f6faf73bc3f4',1,'verb','A1','S1','W1',null,'[{"phrase":"move on","register":null,"definition_en":"to leave your present job , class , or activity and start doing another one","translation":"شغل، کلاس یا فعالیت فعلی خود را ترک کنید و شروع به انجام یکی دیگر کنید","example":"I enjoyed my job, but it was time to move on.","example_translation":"از کارم لذت بردم، اما وقت آن رسیده بود که ادامه دهم.","example_audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001555396.mp3"},{"phrase":"get moving","register":"spoken","definition_en":"used to tell someone to hurry","translation":"به کسی میگفت عجله کن","example":"Come on, get moving or you’ll be late for school.","example_translation":"بیا حرکت کن وگرنه دیر به مدرسه میرسی.","example_audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001555335.mp3"},{"phrase":"move with the times","register":null,"definition_en":"to change the way you think and behave , as society changes","translation":"با تغییر جامعه، طرز فکر و رفتار خود را تغییر دهید","example":"If the resorts want to keep attracting tourists, they need to move with the times.","example_translation":"اگر استراحتگاه ها می خواهند به جذب گردشگران ادامه دهند، باید با زمان حرکت کنند.","example_audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001555355.mp3"}]'::jsonb),
('c184b9a6-5921-5b8f-ac7d-950519b6bad6','3b1d659c-6230-5724-8163-f6faf73bc3f4',2,'noun','A1','S2','W1','[ countable ]','[{"phrase":"be on the move","register":null,"definition_en":"to be travelling from one place to another","translation":"از مکانی به مکان دیگر سفر کنید","example":"The rebel army is on the move.","example_translation":"ارتش شورشی در حال حرکت است.","example_audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000193957.mp3"},{"phrase":"get a move on","register":"spoken","definition_en":"used to tell someone to hurry","translation":"به کسی میگفت عجله کن","example":"","example_translation":"","example_audio_url":""},{"phrase":"make the first move","register":null,"definition_en":"to be the person who starts to do something when someone else is too nervous , embarrassed etc to do it","translation":"کسی باشید که وقتی کسی دیگر خیلی عصبی است، خجالت می کشد، شروع به انجام کاری می کند","example":"He was glad she had made the first move and kissed him.","example_translation":"او خوشحال بود که او اولین حرکت را انجام داده بود و او را بوسید.","example_audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001259331.mp3"},{"phrase":"make a move","register":"informal","definition_en":"to leave a place","translation":"برای ترک یک مکان","example":"It’s getting late – we ought to make a move.","example_translation":"دیر شده است - ما باید حرکتی انجام دهیم.","example_audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001555482.mp3"}]'::jsonb),
('2fa87e36-0303-587a-b481-c11a170202af','0653147a-a1d6-5ca5-992f-09652b785fd1',1,'adverb','A1','S1','W1',null,'[{"phrase":"much less","register":null,"definition_en":"used to say that a greater thing is even less true, likely, or possible than the thing you have just mentioned","translation":"قبلاً می گفت که یک چیز بزرگتر حتی کمتر از چیزی که ذکر کردید درست، محتمل یا ممکن است","example":"The shelves were lined with books which neither Hugo nor Sally would ever open, much less read.","example_translation":"قفسه‌ها مملو از کتاب‌هایی بود که نه هوگو و نه سالی هرگز آن‌ها را باز نمی‌کردند.","example_audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001821343.mp3"},{"phrase":"much as","register":null,"definition_en":"although","translation":"اگرچه","example":"Much as I like Bob, I wouldn’t want to live with him.","example_translation":"همان‌قدر که باب را دوست دارم، نمی‌خواهم با او زندگی کنم.","example_audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000194677.mp3"}]'::jsonb),
('f60bea68-b34a-5d29-b856-5586b29ab383','0653147a-a1d6-5ca5-992f-09652b785fd1',2,'determiner','A1','S1','W1',null,'[{"phrase":"as much","register":null,"definition_en":"an amount that is equal and not less","translation":"مقداری که مساوی باشد و کمتر نباشد","example":"I hope you have as much fun as I did.","example_translation":"امیدوارم شما هم مثل من لذت ببرید.","example_audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001821366.mp3"},{"phrase":"not be much of a something","register":null,"definition_en":"to not be a good example of something or not be very good at something","translation":"مثال خوبی برای چیزی نباشیم یا در چیزی خیلی خوب نباشیم","example":"I’m not much of a dancer, I’m afraid.","example_translation":"من زیاد اهل رقص نیستم، می ترسم.","example_audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000194837.mp3"},{"phrase":"be too much for somebody","register":null,"definition_en":"to be too difficult for someone to do or bear","translation":"انجام دادن یا تحمل کردن برای کسی خیلی سخت است","example":"The effort of climbing the stairs had been too much for the old man.","example_translation":"تلاش برای بالا رفتن از پله ها برای پیرمرد زیاد بود.","example_audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000194847.mp3"},{"phrase":"not be up to much","register":"spoken","definition_en":"to be fairly bad","translation":"نسبتا بد بودن","example":"The restaurant’s very grand but the food isn’t up to much.","example_translation":"رستوران بسیار بزرگ است، اما غذا زیاد نیست.","example_audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000194832.mp3"},{"phrase":"there is not much in it","register":"informal","definition_en":"used to say that there is little difference between two things or amounts","translation":"می گفت که تفاوت کمی بین دو چیز یا مقدار وجود دارد","example":"‘Isn’t the woollen carpet more expensive?’ ‘A little, perhaps, but there’s not much in it.’","example_translation":"«آیا فرش پشمی گران‌تر نیست؟» «شاید کمی، اما چیز زیادی در آن نیست.»","example_audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001821386.mp3"},{"phrase":"so much for something","register":null,"definition_en":"used to say that a particular action, idea, statement etc was not useful or did not produce the result that was hoped for","translation":"معمولاً می‌گفتند که یک عمل، ایده، بیانیه و غیره خاص مفید نبوده یا نتیجه‌ای را که انتظار می‌رفت به بار نمی‌آورد","example":"He’s late again. So much for good intentions.","example_translation":"او دوباره دیر کرد خیلی برای نیت خوب.","example_audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001837452.mp3"},{"phrase":"as much again","register":null,"definition_en":"an additional amount that is equal","translation":"مقدار اضافی که برابر است","example":"The car only cost me £1,500 but it cost as much again to get it insured.","example_translation":"این ماشین فقط 1500 پوند برای من هزینه داشت اما دوباره به همان اندازه برای بیمه کردنش هزینه کرد.","example_audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000194894.mp3"}]'::jsonb),
