('72cc7580-4861-5c8f-8465-1acce093c271','9392b831-cbd7-5d36-a859-e59a66d28d00',22,'card game','بازی با ورق','spoken & written','to play a particular card as your first card in one part of a card game','[ intransitive, transitive ]',null,'برای بازی یک کارت خاص به عنوان اولین کارت خود در بخشی از یک بازی ورق','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('e3c03331-6cf9-566b-b3bd-9add5c4c5c5c','7b1c0ef9-4d53-5520-9f3a-6123d7d4f34d',1,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'the lead','پیشتازی، پیشروی؛ سرب (فلز)؛ خط (ماشین)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['be in the lead He was in the lead after the first lap of the race.','have the lead He has a one-shot lead in the golf tournament.','take the lead (= start being in the lead instead of someone else ) Lewis Hamilton has just taken the lead in the Monaco Grand Prix.','put somebody in the lead (= make someone be in the lead ) Ronaldo’s goal put Portugal in the lead.','give somebody the lead (= make someone be in the lead ) A goal in the 10th minute gave England the lead.','extend/increase/stretch somebody’s lead (= make the lead bigger ) The Australian rugby team extended its lead with a try from Stirling Mortlock.','throw away a lead (= to lose the lead ) Arsenal threw away a two-goal lead.','blow a lead informal (= to lose the lead ) They managed to blow a 22-point lead.','share the lead (= when more than one player or team is in the lead ) At the end of the first round, two golfers share the lead.','a big lead The Bruins had a big lead at half-time.','a clear lead The ruling Labour Party has a clear lead in the opinion polls.','a comfortable lead (= a big lead ) The Wildcats had a comfortable lead in the first half.','a commanding lead (= a big lead ) Alonso raced into a commanding lead.','an early lead (= a lead early in a game, election etc ) Liverpool took an early lead with a goal from Steven Gerrard.','a one-shot/two-goal/three point etc lead (= a lead of a specific amount ) Goals by Keane and Lennon gave Tottenham a two-goal lead.']::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('011f1182-6b3a-56ec-b443-a7dd5eeb4cde','7b1c0ef9-4d53-5520-9f3a-6123d7d4f34d',2,null,null,'spoken & written','the amount or distance by which one competitor is ahead of another','[ singular ]',null,'مقدار یا فاصله ای که یک رقیب از رقیب دیگر جلوتر است','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['be in the lead He was in the lead after the first lap of the race.','have the lead He has a one-shot lead in the golf tournament.','take the lead (= start being in the lead instead of someone else ) Lewis Hamilton has just taken the lead in the Monaco Grand Prix.','put somebody in the lead (= make someone be in the lead ) Ronaldo’s goal put Portugal in the lead.','give somebody the lead (= make someone be in the lead ) A goal in the 10th minute gave England the lead.','extend/increase/stretch somebody’s lead (= make the lead bigger ) The Australian rugby team extended its lead with a try from Stirling Mortlock.','throw away a lead (= to lose the lead ) Arsenal threw away a two-goal lead.','blow a lead informal (= to lose the lead ) They managed to blow a 22-point lead.','share the lead (= when more than one player or team is in the lead ) At the end of the first round, two golfers share the lead.','a big lead The Bruins had a big lead at half-time.','a clear lead The ruling Labour Party has a clear lead in the opinion polls.','a comfortable lead (= a big lead ) The Wildcats had a comfortable lead in the first half.','a commanding lead (= a big lead ) Alonso raced into a commanding lead.','an early lead (= a lead early in a game, election etc ) Liverpool took an early lead with a goal from Steven Gerrard.','a one-shot/two-goal/three point etc lead (= a lead of a specific amount ) Goals by Keane and Lennon gave Tottenham a two-goal lead.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"The Chicago Bulls had a narrow lead (= were winning by a small number of points ) .","translation":"شیکاگو بولز یک برتری کم داشت (= با تعداد کمی امتیاز برنده می شد).","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001802787.mp3"},{"sentence":"The Socialists now have a commanding lead over their opponents.","translation":"سوسیالیست ها اکنون برتری بزرگی نسبت به مخالفان خود دارند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001802794.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('f500cb6f-1f60-5a3b-8245-fb92848a7cad','7b1c0ef9-4d53-5520-9f3a-6123d7d4f34d',3,null,null,'spoken & written','if someone follows someone else’s lead, they do the same as the other person has done','[ singular ]',null,'اگر کسی از دیگران پیروی کند، همان کاری را انجام می دهد که شخص دیگر انجام داده است','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['be in the lead He was in the lead after the first lap of the race.','have the lead He has a one-shot lead in the golf tournament.','take the lead (= start being in the lead instead of someone else ) Lewis Hamilton has just taken the lead in the Monaco Grand Prix.','put somebody in the lead (= make someone be in the lead ) Ronaldo’s goal put Portugal in the lead.','give somebody the lead (= make someone be in the lead ) A goal in the 10th minute gave England the lead.','extend/increase/stretch somebody’s lead (= make the lead bigger ) The Australian rugby team extended its lead with a try from Stirling Mortlock.','throw away a lead (= to lose the lead ) Arsenal threw away a two-goal lead.','blow a lead informal (= to lose the lead ) They managed to blow a 22-point lead.','share the lead (= when more than one player or team is in the lead ) At the end of the first round, two golfers share the lead.','a big lead The Bruins had a big lead at half-time.','a clear lead The ruling Labour Party has a clear lead in the opinion polls.','a comfortable lead (= a big lead ) The Wildcats had a comfortable lead in the first half.','a commanding lead (= a big lead ) Alonso raced into a commanding lead.','an early lead (= a lead early in a game, election etc ) Liverpool took an early lead with a goal from Steven Gerrard.','a one-shot/two-goal/three point etc lead (= a lead of a specific amount ) Goals by Keane and Lennon gave Tottenham a two-goal lead.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"Other countries are likely to follow the U.S.''s lead .","translation":"سایر کشورها احتمالاً از ایالات متحده پیروی خواهند کرد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001488397.mp3"},{"sentence":"The Government should give industry a lead in tackling racism (= show what other people should do ) .","translation":"دولت باید در مقابله با نژادپرستی به صنعت پیشتاز باشد (= نشان دهد که دیگران چه کاری باید انجام دهند).","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001488394.mp3"},{"sentence":"The black population in the 1960s looked to Ali for a lead (= looked to him to show them what they should do ) .","translation":"جمعیت سیاه‌پوست در دهه 1960 به علی نگاه می‌کردند (= به او نگاه می‌کردند تا به آنها نشان دهد چه باید بکنند).","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001802807.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
