('44bdfa96-7699-5585-8aca-3284e2e37d75','fa115472-9e67-5124-902a-28cf5689b8ac',1,'success','موفقیت','spoken & written','good things that happen to you by chance',null,null,'شانس، اقبال؛ بخت (خوش)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['good luck These birds are said to bring good luck.','bad luck His bad luck continued.','sheer/pure luck (= chance, and not skill or effort ) She managed to catch hold of the rope by sheer luck.','dumb luck American English (= sheer good luck, not influenced by anything you did ) Sometimes I think my success was really just dumb luck.','beginner’s luck (= good luck that happens when you first try something ) He’d hit the center of the target. ‘Beginner’s luck, I guess, ’ he said.','have good/bad luck I’ve had a bit of bad luck.','have more/less luck I hope you have more luck in the next competition.','have no luck ( also not have much/any luck ) (= not be lucky or successful ) I’d been looking for a job for weeks, but had had no luck.','can’t believe your luck I couldn’t believe my luck as my number was called out!','have the (good/bad) luck to do something He had the good luck to meet a man who could help him.','somebody’s luck holds (= they continue having good luck ) Our luck held, and the weather remained fine.','somebody’s luck runs out (= they stop having good luck ) Finally my luck ran out and they caught me.','bring somebody (good/bad) luck He always carried the stone in his pocket; he reckoned it brought him luck.','a piece/stroke of luck (= something good that happens by chance ) What a piece of luck that he arrived when he did!','a run of good/bad luck (= a series of good or bad things ) The team has had a run of bad luck lately, losing their last five games.','a matter of luck (= something that depends on chance ) Winning is a matter of luck.','an element of luck (= an amount of luck that is involved in something ) There is always an element of luck when hiring someone for a job.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"You’re not having much luck today, are you?","translation":"امروز شانس زیادی ندارید، نه؟","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001473681.mp3"},{"sentence":"He’s had good luck with his roses this year.","translation":"او امسال با گل های رزش خوش شانس بوده است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001972206.mp3"},{"sentence":"It was an incredible piece of luck.","translation":"این یک شانس باورنکردنی بود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001972218.mp3"},{"sentence":"It was only by luck that they managed to avoid hitting the rocks near the shore.","translation":"فقط با شانس بود که آنها موفق شدند از برخورد به صخره های نزدیک ساحل اجتناب کنند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa000977.mp3"}]'::jsonb,4),
('e55e582d-7666-54d0-939f-0d07c368d7a6','fa115472-9e67-5124-902a-28cf5689b8ac',2,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'bad luck','شانس، اقبال؛ بخت (خوش)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['good luck These birds are said to bring good luck.','bad luck His bad luck continued.','sheer/pure luck (= chance, and not skill or effort ) She managed to catch hold of the rope by sheer luck.','dumb luck American English (= sheer good luck, not influenced by anything you did ) Sometimes I think my success was really just dumb luck.','beginner’s luck (= good luck that happens when you first try something ) He’d hit the center of the target. ‘Beginner’s luck, I guess, ’ he said.','have good/bad luck I’ve had a bit of bad luck.','have more/less luck I hope you have more luck in the next competition.','have no luck ( also not have much/any luck ) (= not be lucky or successful ) I’d been looking for a job for weeks, but had had no luck.','can’t believe your luck I couldn’t believe my luck as my number was called out!','have the (good/bad) luck to do something He had the good luck to meet a man who could help him.','somebody’s luck holds (= they continue having good luck ) Our luck held, and the weather remained fine.','somebody’s luck runs out (= they stop having good luck ) Finally my luck ran out and they caught me.','bring somebody (good/bad) luck He always carried the stone in his pocket; he reckoned it brought him luck.','a piece/stroke of luck (= something good that happens by chance ) What a piece of luck that he arrived when he did!','a run of good/bad luck (= a series of good or bad things ) The team has had a run of bad luck lately, losing their last five games.','a matter of luck (= something that depends on chance ) Winning is a matter of luck.','an element of luck (= an amount of luck that is involved in something ) There is always an element of luck when hiring someone for a job.']::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('986b77d4-0155-555b-82b5-fda0669cf6dc','fa115472-9e67-5124-902a-28cf5689b8ac',3,'chance','شانس','spoken & written','when good or bad things happen to people by chance',null,null,'وقتی اتفاقات خوب یا بد برای مردم اتفاق می افتد','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['good luck These birds are said to bring good luck.','bad luck His bad luck continued.','sheer/pure luck (= chance, and not skill or effort ) She managed to catch hold of the rope by sheer luck.','dumb luck American English (= sheer good luck, not influenced by anything you did ) Sometimes I think my success was really just dumb luck.','beginner’s luck (= good luck that happens when you first try something ) He’d hit the center of the target. ‘Beginner’s luck, I guess, ’ he said.','have good/bad luck I’ve had a bit of bad luck.','have more/less luck I hope you have more luck in the next competition.','have no luck ( also not have much/any luck ) (= not be lucky or successful ) I’d been looking for a job for weeks, but had had no luck.','can’t believe your luck I couldn’t believe my luck as my number was called out!','have the (good/bad) luck to do something He had the good luck to meet a man who could help him.','somebody’s luck holds (= they continue having good luck ) Our luck held, and the weather remained fine.','somebody’s luck runs out (= they stop having good luck ) Finally my luck ran out and they caught me.','bring somebody (good/bad) luck He always carried the stone in his pocket; he reckoned it brought him luck.','a piece/stroke of luck (= something good that happens by chance ) What a piece of luck that he arrived when he did!','a run of good/bad luck (= a series of good or bad things ) The team has had a run of bad luck lately, losing their last five games.','a matter of luck (= something that depends on chance ) Winning is a matter of luck.','an element of luck (= an amount of luck that is involved in something ) There is always an element of luck when hiring someone for a job.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"Roulette is a game of luck.","translation":"رولت یک بازی شانس است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001739417.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
