('7655be9c-7cc5-55ac-9356-609dbf70b574','58063c55-4c82-50ec-8bdb-e5e29b19f69d',9,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'needs must (when the devil drives)','نیاز، احتیاج؛ ضرورت؛ فقر (نیاز)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['a real/clear need (= one that really exists ) There is a real need for after-school care in our area.','an urgent need (= one that must be dealt with quickly ) The most urgent need was for more teachers.','a pressing/crying need (= a very urgent need ) There’s a crying need for more doctors and nurses.','a desperate need (= an extremely urgent need ) There is a desperate need to build more housing.','a growing/increasing need She emphasized the growing need to deal with environmental problems.','stress/emphasize/underline the need for something (= say how important it is ) He stressed the need for better training courses.','eliminate the need for something ( also obviate the need for something formal ) (= make something unnecessary ) The new drug treatment eliminates the need for surgery.','a need exists New teaching materials must be created if a need exists for them.','there is a need for something Clearly there is a need for more research.','there is no need for something They felt that there was no need for a formal contract.','as/if/when the need arises (= if or when something becomes necessary ) Team members move from job to job as the need arises.','if need be (= if it is necessary ) I can work during my lunch break if need be.']::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('d27276a6-d324-5ceb-adf9-69bc6a2f54e5','2690e6a6-7f06-5a64-b8d3-a788fcba5f04',1,null,null,'spoken & written','information about something that has happened recently',null,null,'خبر، اخبار؛ خبر (خوب)؛ پخش (خبر)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['good news He’s feeling much better, so that’s good news.','great/wonderful news They’re getting married? That’s wonderful news!','welcome news (= good news that makes you happy ) The lower interest rates will be welcome news to home owners.','bad/terrible news ‘I’m afraid I have bad news, ’ said Jackson. Have you heard the terrible news about Simon?','the latest news Mom sent a letter with all the latest news.','old news (= news that you have already heard ) She wasn’t surprised; it was old news to her.','important news I’ve got some important news to tell you.','the big news informal (= an important piece of news ) The big news is that Polly and Richard are going to get married.','have some news (for somebody) I could tell by his face that he had some news.','tell somebody the news Jack called him to tell him the good news.','break the news (to somebody) (= tell someone some bad news ) Two policemen came to the door to break the news about her husband.','spread the news (= tell a lot of people the news ) After she had the baby, her husband made phone calls to spread the happy news.','hear the news (= hear about something that has happened ) She was really upset when she heard the news.','welcome the news formal (= say that you are pleased about some news ) Environmental groups welcomed the news that the area would be protected.','greet the news with surprise/delight etc formal (= react to the news in a particular way ) Fans greeted the news of the victory with a loud cheer.','news spreads (= a lot of people find out the news from other people ) News spreads fast in a small town.','a piece of news ( also a bit of news British English ) Leo thought about this piece of news carefully.','the good news is …/the bad news is ... (= used to introduce a piece of good and bad news ) The good news is that most stores have the game in stock; the bad news is that it’s not cheap.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"I hope to have some good news for you soon.","translation":"امیدوارم به زودی خبرهای خوبی برای شما داشته باشم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa001095.mp3"},{"sentence":"We are delighted at the news that our daughter is expecting a baby.","translation":"ما از این خبر که دخترمان در انتظار بچه دار شدن است خوشحالیم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001964354.mp3"},{"sentence":"What’s the latest news on your university application?","translation":"آخرین اخبار درخواست دانشگاه شما چیست؟","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001964364.mp3"},{"sentence":"Everyone is shocked by the news of the arrests.","translation":"همه از خبر دستگیری ها شوکه شده اند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001964378.mp3"}]'::jsonb,4),
('1bf9a573-d349-564f-8461-dbeba2a54108','2690e6a6-7f06-5a64-b8d3-a788fcba5f04',2,null,null,'spoken & written','reports of recent events in the newspapers or on the radio or television',null,null,'گزارش رویدادهای اخیر در روزنامه ها یا رادیو یا تلویزیون','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['good news He’s feeling much better, so that’s good news.','great/wonderful news They’re getting married? That’s wonderful news!','welcome news (= good news that makes you happy ) The lower interest rates will be welcome news to home owners.','bad/terrible news ‘I’m afraid I have bad news, ’ said Jackson. Have you heard the terrible news about Simon?','the latest news Mom sent a letter with all the latest news.','old news (= news that you have already heard ) She wasn’t surprised; it was old news to her.','important news I’ve got some important news to tell you.','the big news informal (= an important piece of news ) The big news is that Polly and Richard are going to get married.','have some news (for somebody) I could tell by his face that he had some news.','tell somebody the news Jack called him to tell him the good news.','break the news (to somebody) (= tell someone some bad news ) Two policemen came to the door to break the news about her husband.','spread the news (= tell a lot of people the news ) After she had the baby, her husband made phone calls to spread the happy news.','hear the news (= hear about something that has happened ) She was really upset when she heard the news.','welcome the news formal (= say that you are pleased about some news ) Environmental groups welcomed the news that the area would be protected.','greet the news with surprise/delight etc formal (= react to the news in a particular way ) Fans greeted the news of the victory with a loud cheer.','news spreads (= a lot of people find out the news from other people ) News spreads fast in a small town.','a piece of news ( also a bit of news British English ) Leo thought about this piece of news carefully.','the good news is …/the bad news is ... (= used to introduce a piece of good and bad news ) The good news is that most stores have the game in stock; the bad news is that it’s not cheap.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"a late evening news broadcast","translation":"پخش خبری اواخر عصر","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001556518.mp3"},{"sentence":"We’ve got the news headlines coming up at half past twelve.","translation":"ما تیترهای اخبار را در ساعت دوازده و نیم داریم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001556521.mp3"},{"sentence":"a news and current affairs programme","translation":"یک برنامه اخبار و امور جاری","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001556525.mp3"},{"sentence":"Here’s the sports news from Jane Murray.","translation":"در اینجا اخبار ورزشی از جین موری است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001556531.mp3"},{"sentence":"the latest news from the Olympic stadium","translation":"آخرین اخبار ورزشگاه المپیک","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001556533.mp3"},{"sentence":"news on the latest developments in the talks","translation":"اخبار آخرین تحولات مذاکرات","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001556528.mp3"},{"sentence":"Several evening papers carried the news that a cabinet minister was about to resign.","translation":"چند روزنامه عصر خبر می دادند که یکی از وزیران کابینه در شرف استعفا است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001760819.mp3"},{"sentence":"Twenty years ago environmental issues rarely made the news (= were rarely considered important enough to be in the news ) .","translation":"بیست سال پیش، مسائل زیست محیطی به ندرت خبرساز می شد (= به ندرت آنقدر مهم در نظر گرفته می شد که در اخبار باشد).","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000240906.mp3"},{"sentence":"Hong Kong is in the news this morning.","translation":"هنگ کنگ امروز صبح در اخبار است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001556539.mp3"},{"sentence":"His resignation was front page news (= was important news ) .","translation":"استعفای او خبر صفحه اول بود (= خبر مهم بود).","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001556543.mp3"},{"sentence":"Never before has a news story triggered such sensational sales of the newspaper.","translation":"پیش از این هرگز یک خبر باعث فروش این چنین پر شور روزنامه نشده بود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000240916.mp3"}]'::jsonb,11),
('4bbca970-ff30-57cf-b8df-ef1b6569c87b','2690e6a6-7f06-5a64-b8d3-a788fcba5f04',3,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'the news','خبر، اخبار؛ خبر (خوب)؛ پخش (خبر)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['good news He’s feeling much better, so that’s good news.','great/wonderful news They’re getting married? That’s wonderful news!','welcome news (= good news that makes you happy ) The lower interest rates will be welcome news to home owners.','bad/terrible news ‘I’m afraid I have bad news, ’ said Jackson. Have you heard the terrible news about Simon?','the latest news Mom sent a letter with all the latest news.','old news (= news that you have already heard ) She wasn’t surprised; it was old news to her.','important news I’ve got some important news to tell you.','the big news informal (= an important piece of news ) The big news is that Polly and Richard are going to get married.','have some news (for somebody) I could tell by his face that he had some news.','tell somebody the news Jack called him to tell him the good news.','break the news (to somebody) (= tell someone some bad news ) Two policemen came to the door to break the news about her husband.','spread the news (= tell a lot of people the news ) After she had the baby, her husband made phone calls to spread the happy news.','hear the news (= hear about something that has happened ) She was really upset when she heard the news.','welcome the news formal (= say that you are pleased about some news ) Environmental groups welcomed the news that the area would be protected.','greet the news with surprise/delight etc formal (= react to the news in a particular way ) Fans greeted the news of the victory with a loud cheer.','news spreads (= a lot of people find out the news from other people ) News spreads fast in a small town.','a piece of news ( also a bit of news British English ) Leo thought about this piece of news carefully.','the good news is …/the bad news is ... (= used to introduce a piece of good and bad news ) The good news is that most stores have the game in stock; the bad news is that it’s not cheap.']::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
