('c7756c96-d049-50ef-9444-cca4a5603ac8','c28f297e-f745-5c4c-acf1-d1663b70020e',1,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'the past','گذشته، تاریخچه (فرد)؛ گذشته (دردسر)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['the recent past The optimistic economic climate of the recent past has gone.','the distant/remote past Rivers of molten lava clearly flowed here in the distant past.','the immediate past (= the very recent past ) In order to understand the present, we must look at the immediate past.','forget the past Forget the past and focus on the future.','be living in the past (= think only about the past ) You’ve got to stop living in the past.','be/become a thing of the past (= not exist anymore, or stop existing ) We hope that smoking will become a thing of the past.','a break with the past (= when something is done in a completely different way to how it was done in the past ) These policies are a break with the past.','in the dim and distant past (= a very long time ago ) I think she sang Ireland''s entry in the Eurovision Song Contest sometime in the dim and distant past.']::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('d9a41b98-6dc3-5db9-8085-e159a5fe3b42','c28f297e-f745-5c4c-acf1-d1663b70020e',2,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'all in the past','گذشته، تاریخچه (فرد)؛ گذشته (دردسر)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['the recent past The optimistic economic climate of the recent past has gone.','the distant/remote past Rivers of molten lava clearly flowed here in the distant past.','the immediate past (= the very recent past ) In order to understand the present, we must look at the immediate past.','forget the past Forget the past and focus on the future.','be living in the past (= think only about the past ) You’ve got to stop living in the past.','be/become a thing of the past (= not exist anymore, or stop existing ) We hope that smoking will become a thing of the past.','a break with the past (= when something is done in a completely different way to how it was done in the past ) These policies are a break with the past.','in the dim and distant past (= a very long time ago ) I think she sang Ireland''s entry in the Eurovision Song Contest sometime in the dim and distant past.']::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('8c43835d-c1dc-5602-bea5-3d44c54cc1a3','c28f297e-f745-5c4c-acf1-d1663b70020e',3,null,null,'spoken & written','the past life or existence of someone or something','[ singular ]',null,'زندگی یا وجود گذشته کسی یا چیزی','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['the recent past The optimistic economic climate of the recent past has gone.','the distant/remote past Rivers of molten lava clearly flowed here in the distant past.','the immediate past (= the very recent past ) In order to understand the present, we must look at the immediate past.','forget the past Forget the past and focus on the future.','be living in the past (= think only about the past ) You’ve got to stop living in the past.','be/become a thing of the past (= not exist anymore, or stop existing ) We hope that smoking will become a thing of the past.','a break with the past (= when something is done in a completely different way to how it was done in the past ) These policies are a break with the past.','in the dim and distant past (= a very long time ago ) I think she sang Ireland''s entry in the Eurovision Song Contest sometime in the dim and distant past.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"At some time in its past the church was rebuilt.","translation":"در زمانی در گذشته کلیسا بازسازی شد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000371774.mp3"},{"sentence":"The woman who ran the bar had a very shady past (= events in her past which might be considered bad ) .","translation":"زنی که بار را اداره می کرد گذشته ای بسیار مشکوک داشت (= رویدادهایی در گذشته او که ممکن است بد تلقی شوند).","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001583964.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('b894ea5e-c630-5e34-9341-52bd51ea3dcc','644c4520-566b-5850-89fe-af2a68e605ca',1,'track','مسیر','spoken & written','a track that has been made deliberately or made by many people walking over the same ground',null,null,'مسیر، گذرگاه؛ مسیر (زندگی)؛ راه (بدن)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['follow a path We followed a path through the trees.','take a path (= start going along it ) Take the wide path to the right.','keep to the path They kept carefully to the paths and did not go across the farmer''s fields.','a path leads somewhere There are many paths leading to the top of the mountain.','a path winds A narrow path wound down towards the beach.','a path climbs (= goes upwards ) I could see the line of a path that climbed up from the bay.','narrow We walked along a narrow path beside a stream.','steep A steep path led down to the harbour.','muddy They trudged up the muddy path.','rocky Our guide trod carefully down the rocky path.','winding He climbed the winding path up the hill.','well-worn (= used a lot or for a long time ) I followed what seemed to be a well-worn path heading in the right direction.','a garden path Emma came running up the garden path.','a coast/coastal/cliff path From the cliff path, you get superb views out to sea.','a cycle path (= for people riding bicycles ) They should put a cycle path along the edge of each new road they build.','a bridle path (= for people riding horses ) He knows all the bridle paths through the woods.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"I walked nervously up the garden path towards the front door.","translation":"عصبی از مسیر باغ به سمت در ورودی رفتم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000372773.mp3"},{"sentence":"a well-worn path across the grass","translation":"مسیری فرسوده در میان چمن","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000372774.mp3"},{"sentence":"Follow the path along the river to the bridge.","translation":"مسیر کنار رودخانه تا پل را دنبال کنید.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001584068.mp3"},{"sentence":"a path leading to the summer house","translation":"مسیری که به خانه تابستانی منتهی می شود","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001584071.mp3"}]'::jsonb,4),
