('937e0353-3abc-50e1-bfcf-a0f31b1605e1','2bc2c248-3ae7-5d02-8354-e7d16bbb52c5',1,null,null,'spoken & written','someone from Poland',null,null,'کسی از لهستان','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('b16ccb6c-f480-545f-b387-1483b1cdf2d3','b71b6251-d8f3-5234-bbea-21ecd0312186',1,null,null,'spoken & written','the process of finding out what people think about something by asking many people the same question , or the record of the result','[ countable ]',null,'نظرسنجی، نظرسنجی (افکار)؛ رأی‌گیری',array['opinion poll','survey']::text[],'{}'::text[],array['carry out/take/do a poll A similar poll was carried out among academics in the United States. A poll taken last month gave the Democrats a seven-point lead.','conduct a poll formal (= carry out a poll ) The poll was conducted with a sample of 1,023 adults.','a poll shows/indicates/suggests something Polls show that older voters are most concerned about economic issues.','a poll finds something Our poll found that 29 percent rated his performance as good.','poll results/findings The poll results are very encouraging.','a poll rating (= showing how popular someone is ) His poll ratings keep slipping.','an opinion poll (= that measures what people think about something ) A recent opinion poll showed strong support for the government.','an exit poll (= when people are asked how they have just voted ) The exit polls said that 46 percent of women had voted for Obama.','a popularity poll (= measuring how popular someone is ) In most popularity polls, he is in fourth or fifth place.','a local/national/statewide etc poll Local polls show him leading by only two or three points.','somebody’s lead in the polls Labour soon regained its lead in the polls.','somebody’s standing in the polls (= how popular a poll shows them to be ) The president''s standing in the polls declined sharply.','be ahead/leading in the polls The good news is that we are ahead in the polls.','be behind/trailing in the polls At the moment the Democrats are trailing in the polls.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"A recent poll found that 80% of Californians support the governor.","translation":"یک نظرسنجی اخیر نشان داد که 80 درصد از مردم کالیفرنیا از فرماندار حمایت می کنند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001574173.mp3"},{"sentence":"Polls indicate that education is the top issue with voters.","translation":"نظرسنجی‌ها نشان می‌دهد که آموزش مهمترین مسئله رای دهندگان است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001574177.mp3"},{"sentence":"Labour is ahead in the polls.","translation":"حزب کارگر در نظرسنجی ها پیشتاز است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001764423.mp3"},{"sentence":"The latest public opinion poll showed that 25% of us consider ourselves superstitious.","translation":"آخرین نظرسنجی عمومی نشان داد که 25 درصد از ما خود را خرافاتی می دانیم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001574180.mp3"},{"sentence":"a poll conducted by ‘USA Today’","translation":"نظرسنجی انجام شده توسط USA Today","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000346139.mp3"},{"sentence":"a poll on eating habits","translation":"یک نظرسنجی در مورد عادات غذایی","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001574186.mp3"},{"sentence":"a poll of 1,000 people","translation":"نظرسنجی از 1000 نفر","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001574189.mp3"}]'::jsonb,7),
('0335039e-e0e5-536e-8394-8b89c45b6cfd','b71b6251-d8f3-5234-bbea-21ecd0312186',2,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'go to the polls','نظرسنجی، نظرسنجی (افکار)؛ رأی‌گیری','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['carry out/take/do a poll A similar poll was carried out among academics in the United States. A poll taken last month gave the Democrats a seven-point lead.','conduct a poll formal (= carry out a poll ) The poll was conducted with a sample of 1,023 adults.','a poll shows/indicates/suggests something Polls show that older voters are most concerned about economic issues.','a poll finds something Our poll found that 29 percent rated his performance as good.','poll results/findings The poll results are very encouraging.','a poll rating (= showing how popular someone is ) His poll ratings keep slipping.','an opinion poll (= that measures what people think about something ) A recent opinion poll showed strong support for the government.','an exit poll (= when people are asked how they have just voted ) The exit polls said that 46 percent of women had voted for Obama.','a popularity poll (= measuring how popular someone is ) In most popularity polls, he is in fourth or fifth place.','a local/national/statewide etc poll Local polls show him leading by only two or three points.','somebody’s lead in the polls Labour soon regained its lead in the polls.','somebody’s standing in the polls (= how popular a poll shows them to be ) The president''s standing in the polls declined sharply.','be ahead/leading in the polls The good news is that we are ahead in the polls.','be behind/trailing in the polls At the moment the Democrats are trailing in the polls.']::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('6c09fbe0-204a-5882-975b-5b9723008e18','b71b6251-d8f3-5234-bbea-21ecd0312186',3,null,null,'spoken & written','the process of voting in an election , or the number of votes recorded','[ singular ]',null,'روند رای دادن در یک انتخابات، یا تعداد آرای ثبت شده','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['carry out/take/do a poll A similar poll was carried out among academics in the United States. A poll taken last month gave the Democrats a seven-point lead.','conduct a poll formal (= carry out a poll ) The poll was conducted with a sample of 1,023 adults.','a poll shows/indicates/suggests something Polls show that older voters are most concerned about economic issues.','a poll finds something Our poll found that 29 percent rated his performance as good.','poll results/findings The poll results are very encouraging.','a poll rating (= showing how popular someone is ) His poll ratings keep slipping.','an opinion poll (= that measures what people think about something ) A recent opinion poll showed strong support for the government.','an exit poll (= when people are asked how they have just voted ) The exit polls said that 46 percent of women had voted for Obama.','a popularity poll (= measuring how popular someone is ) In most popularity polls, he is in fourth or fifth place.','a local/national/statewide etc poll Local polls show him leading by only two or three points.','somebody’s lead in the polls Labour soon regained its lead in the polls.','somebody’s standing in the polls (= how popular a poll shows them to be ) The president''s standing in the polls declined sharply.','be ahead/leading in the polls The good news is that we are ahead in the polls.','be behind/trailing in the polls At the moment the Democrats are trailing in the polls.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"Labour won the election with 40% of the poll.","translation":"حزب کارگر با کسب 40 درصد آرا در انتخابات پیروز شد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000346171.mp3"},{"sentence":"The result of the poll won’t be known until around midnight.","translation":"نتیجه نظرسنجی تا حدود نیمه شب مشخص نخواهد شد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000346161.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
