('981018d8-05a1-5476-9396-2dc82b48ee3d','b2aa20fc-1f12-5d5a-bba4-e16571a34c23',1,null,null,'spoken & written','to trust or depend on someone or something to do what you need or expect them to do',null,'rely on/upon somebody/something','برای انجام کاری که نیاز دارید یا انتظار دارید به کسی یا چیزی اعتماد کنید یا به او وابسته باشید','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"I knew I could rely on David.","translation":"می دانستم که می توانم به دیوید تکیه کنم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001570413.mp3"},{"sentence":"Many working women rely on relatives to help take care of their children.","translation":"بسیاری از زنان شاغل برای مراقبت از فرزندان خود به اقوام خود متکی هستند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000772627.mp3"},{"sentence":"Many people now rely on the Internet for news.","translation":"اکنون بسیاری از مردم برای دریافت اخبار به اینترنت متکی هستند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000772633.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('1b293012-afd7-5a89-885c-caf835fe2dcf','8f296683-3207-5f35-bf14-0411ca18b58c',1,null,null,'spoken & written','to regularly pay money to live in a house or room that belongs to someone else, or to use something that belongs to someone else','[ intransitive, transitive ]',null,'اجاره کردن؛ درآمد داشتن (از اجاره)؛ اجاره دادن (به)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Most students rent rooms in their second year.","translation":"اکثر دانش آموزان در سال دوم خود اتاق اجاره می کنند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001562434.mp3"},{"sentence":"I’d rather have my own house than rent.","translation":"من ترجیح می دهم خانه خودم را داشته باشم تا اجاره.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001562438.mp3"},{"sentence":"Some farmers rent their land from the council.","translation":"برخی از کشاورزان زمین های خود را از شورا اجاره می دهند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001562441.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('1e7d4338-7b2b-5e00-9da2-6b4b098921d2','8f296683-3207-5f35-bf14-0411ca18b58c',2,null,null,'spoken & written','to let someone live in a house, room etc that you own, or use your land , in return for money','[ transitive ]',null,'به کسی اجازه دهید در ازای پول در خانه، اتاق و غیره که مالک آن هستید زندگی کند یا از زمین شما استفاده کند','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"She rents out two rooms to students.","translation":"او دو اتاق را به دانش آموزان اجاره می دهد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001562446.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('52056371-cec0-5e08-8fc7-93f750432f7b','8f296683-3207-5f35-bf14-0411ca18b58c',3,null,null,'spoken & written','to pay money for the use of something for a short period of time','[ transitive ]',null,'پرداخت پول برای استفاده از چیزی برای مدت کوتاهی','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Will you rent a car while you’re in Spain?","translation":"آیا وقتی در اسپانیا هستید ماشین کرایه می کنید؟","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000775299.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('35a80064-174e-5f8b-a389-b9fa045c025e','1e16da43-0e5e-57b9-bd61-c921cf187d3b',1,null,null,'spoken & written','the money that someone pays regularly to use a room, house etc that belongs to someone else','[ countable, uncountable ]',null,'اجاره، اجاره‌بها؛ اجاره (مال)؛ اجاره (ملک)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['high Rents in the city centre are very high.','low Our workers get low rents and other advantages.','exorbitant (= extremely high ) Some landlords charge exorbitant rents.','fixed The rent is fixed for three years.','affordable (= which people can easily pay ) The government plans to provide more homes at affordable rents.','the annual/monthly/weekly rent Our annual rent is just over $15000.','ground rent British English (= rent paid to the owner of the land that a house, office etc is built on ) There is an additional ground rent of £30 per month.','a peppercorn rent British English (= an extremely low rent ) The colonel let us have the cottage for a peppercorn rent.','back rent (= rent you owe for an earlier period ) Mrs Carr said she is still owed several thousand dollars in back rent.','the rent is due (= it must be paid at a particular time ) The rent is due at the beginning of the week.','pay the rent She couldn’t afford to pay the rent.','increase/raise the rent ( also put up the rent British English ) The landlord wants to put up the rent.','fall behind with the rent/get behind on the rent (= fail to pay your rent on time ) You could be evicted if you fall behind with the rent.','collect the rent His job is to collect the rents from the tenants.','the rent increases/goes up The rent has gone up by over 50% in the last two years.','a rent increase How can they justify such big rent increases?','rent arrears British English (= money that you owe because you have not paid your rent ) The most common debts were rent arrears.','a rent book British English (= a book that shows the payments you have made in rent )']::text[],'[{"sentence":"I pay the rent at the beginning of every month.","translation":"من اول هر ماه اجاره را پرداخت می کنم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001562475.mp3"},{"sentence":"an annual rent of £8,000","translation":"اجاره سالانه 8000 پوند","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001562483.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('1e8fed34-4be4-57ee-bf57-10328c9a7383','1e16da43-0e5e-57b9-bd61-c921cf187d3b',2,null,null,'spoken & written','an amount of money that you pay to use a car, boat etc that belongs to someone else','[ countable, uncountable ]',null,'مقدار پولی که برای استفاده از ماشین، قایق و غیره که متعلق به شخص دیگری است می پردازید','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['high Rents in the city centre are very high.','low Our workers get low rents and other advantages.','exorbitant (= extremely high ) Some landlords charge exorbitant rents.','fixed The rent is fixed for three years.','affordable (= which people can easily pay ) The government plans to provide more homes at affordable rents.','the annual/monthly/weekly rent Our annual rent is just over $15000.','ground rent British English (= rent paid to the owner of the land that a house, office etc is built on ) There is an additional ground rent of £30 per month.','a peppercorn rent British English (= an extremely low rent ) The colonel let us have the cottage for a peppercorn rent.','back rent (= rent you owe for an earlier period ) Mrs Carr said she is still owed several thousand dollars in back rent.','the rent is due (= it must be paid at a particular time ) The rent is due at the beginning of the week.','pay the rent She couldn’t afford to pay the rent.','increase/raise the rent ( also put up the rent British English ) The landlord wants to put up the rent.','fall behind with the rent/get behind on the rent (= fail to pay your rent on time ) You could be evicted if you fall behind with the rent.','collect the rent His job is to collect the rents from the tenants.','the rent increases/goes up The rent has gone up by over 50% in the last two years.','a rent increase How can they justify such big rent increases?','rent arrears British English (= money that you owe because you have not paid your rent ) The most common debts were rent arrears.','a rent book British English (= a book that shows the payments you have made in rent )']::text[],'[{"sentence":"The rent was only $20 an hour.","translation":"اجاره فقط 20 دلار در ساعت بود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001562484.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
