('4fa70540-e49b-5ed2-8fd8-6c69a17605ab','720ac385-e237-56e3-8f9d-604b8d2f6af5',1,'about what is allowed','در مورد آنچه مجاز است','spoken & written','an official instruction that says how things must be done or what is allowed, especially in a game, organization , or job','[ countable ]',null,'قاعده، قانون؛ رول (فیلم)؛ خط (مورب)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['break a rule ( also violate a rule formal ) (= not obey it ) He had clearly broken the official rules. Any one who violates this rule will be severely punished.','obey/follow a rule She wasn’t going to obey their silly rules.','comply with/abide by/observe a rule formal (= obey it ) All members must comply with the rules of the organization. There is little that one country can do if another fails to abide by the rules. We expect you to observe the general rules of conduct as set out below.','stick to/go by the rules informal (= obey them ) We all have to stick to the rules.','make the rules I’m only an assistant manager – I don’t make the rules.','the rule says ... The rule says that you must be standing inside the line.','the rule stipulates that ... formal (= it says that something must be done ) The rules stipulate that clubs must field the strongest team available.','the rule prohibits/forbids something The rule forbids women from becoming members of the club.','the rule requires (that) ... formal (= it says that people must do something ) School rules required all girls to tie back their hair.','the rule applies to somebody/something (= it concerns them ) Everyone thinks that the rule doesn’t apply to them.','play by the rules (= do what is expected and agreed ) The system works well enough — as long as everyone plays by the rules.','bend/stretch the rules (= allow someone to do something that is not normally allowed ) They bend the rules to suit themselves.','relax the rules (= make them less strict ) Britain relaxed its immigration rules.','tighten (up) the rules (= make them stricter ) The EU has tightened the rules on the quality of drinking water.','enforce a rule (= make sure that it is obeyed ) The planning office does not always enforce its own rules.','flout a rule (= break it, without trying to hide what you are doing ) The party continues to flout its own rules.','be bound by rules (= have to obey them ) Solicitors are bound by strict rules that regulate their professional conduct.','strict They have very strict rules about gambling.','simple The rules of the game are quite simple.','petty (= unreasonable rules about unimportant things ) There are hundreds of petty rules.','a school/prison/club etc rule He had broken one of the school rules.','an unwritten rule (= a rule of behaviour that everyone in a group understands ) There’s an unwritten rule that you never call an actor before 10 a.m.','health and safety rules You should follow any health and safety rules which apply to your workplace.','be against the rules (= not be allowed ) It was against the rules to talk in class.','the rules concerning/governing/relating to something formal (= the rules about something ) the rules governing food labeling','a change in the rules I didn’t realise that there had been a change in the rules.','a breach of the rules formal (= something that is against the rules ) a serious breach of the rules','rules and regulations The government keeps introducing more and more rules and regulations.','rules are rules spoken (= a rule must be obeyed ) Rules are rules and you have to abide by them.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"the rules of the game","translation":"قوانین بازی","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa001406.mp3"},{"sentence":"Under the rules, the company must publish its annual accounts.","translation":"طبق قوانین، شرکت باید حساب های سالانه خود را منتشر کند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa001407.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('87cc72b7-6a74-50d1-a886-d6260bf996d7','720ac385-e237-56e3-8f9d-604b8d2f6af5',2,'about what you should do','در مورد آنچه باید انجام دهید','spoken & written','what you should do in a particular situation, or a statement about this','[ countable ]',null,'در یک موقعیت خاص چه کاری باید انجام دهید، یا بیانیه ای در این مورد','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['break a rule ( also violate a rule formal ) (= not obey it ) He had clearly broken the official rules. Any one who violates this rule will be severely punished.','obey/follow a rule She wasn’t going to obey their silly rules.','comply with/abide by/observe a rule formal (= obey it ) All members must comply with the rules of the organization. There is little that one country can do if another fails to abide by the rules. We expect you to observe the general rules of conduct as set out below.','stick to/go by the rules informal (= obey them ) We all have to stick to the rules.','make the rules I’m only an assistant manager – I don’t make the rules.','the rule says ... The rule says that you must be standing inside the line.','the rule stipulates that ... formal (= it says that something must be done ) The rules stipulate that clubs must field the strongest team available.','the rule prohibits/forbids something The rule forbids women from becoming members of the club.','the rule requires (that) ... formal (= it says that people must do something ) School rules required all girls to tie back their hair.','the rule applies to somebody/something (= it concerns them ) Everyone thinks that the rule doesn’t apply to them.','play by the rules (= do what is expected and agreed ) The system works well enough — as long as everyone plays by the rules.','bend/stretch the rules (= allow someone to do something that is not normally allowed ) They bend the rules to suit themselves.','relax the rules (= make them less strict ) Britain relaxed its immigration rules.','tighten (up) the rules (= make them stricter ) The EU has tightened the rules on the quality of drinking water.','enforce a rule (= make sure that it is obeyed ) The planning office does not always enforce its own rules.','flout a rule (= break it, without trying to hide what you are doing ) The party continues to flout its own rules.','be bound by rules (= have to obey them ) Solicitors are bound by strict rules that regulate their professional conduct.','strict They have very strict rules about gambling.','simple The rules of the game are quite simple.','petty (= unreasonable rules about unimportant things ) There are hundreds of petty rules.','a school/prison/club etc rule He had broken one of the school rules.','an unwritten rule (= a rule of behaviour that everyone in a group understands ) There’s an unwritten rule that you never call an actor before 10 a.m.','health and safety rules You should follow any health and safety rules which apply to your workplace.','be against the rules (= not be allowed ) It was against the rules to talk in class.','the rules concerning/governing/relating to something formal (= the rules about something ) the rules governing food labeling','a change in the rules I didn’t realise that there had been a change in the rules.','a breach of the rules formal (= something that is against the rules ) a serious breach of the rules','rules and regulations The government keeps introducing more and more rules and regulations.','rules are rules spoken (= a rule must be obeyed ) Rules are rules and you have to abide by them.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"There are no hard and fast rules (= clear and definite rules ) about what to wear to classes.","translation":"هیچ قانون سخت و سریع (= قوانین واضح و مشخص) در مورد لباس پوشیدن در کلاس ها وجود ندارد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000733922.mp3"},{"sentence":"There are two basic rules of survival.","translation":"دو قانون اساسی برای بقا وجود دارد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001588093.mp3"},{"sentence":"The rule is : if you feel any pain you should stop exercising immediately.","translation":"قانون این است: اگر احساس درد کردید باید فورا ورزش را متوقف کنید.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001774772.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('a6671c0d-0968-520a-a558-f3dce992afbc','720ac385-e237-56e3-8f9d-604b8d2f6af5',3,'normal/usual','عادی/معمول','spoken & written','something that is normal or usually true','[ singular ]',null,'چیزی که طبیعی است یا معمولاً درست است','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['break a rule ( also violate a rule formal ) (= not obey it ) He had clearly broken the official rules. Any one who violates this rule will be severely punished.','obey/follow a rule She wasn’t going to obey their silly rules.','comply with/abide by/observe a rule formal (= obey it ) All members must comply with the rules of the organization. There is little that one country can do if another fails to abide by the rules. We expect you to observe the general rules of conduct as set out below.','stick to/go by the rules informal (= obey them ) We all have to stick to the rules.','make the rules I’m only an assistant manager – I don’t make the rules.','the rule says ... The rule says that you must be standing inside the line.','the rule stipulates that ... formal (= it says that something must be done ) The rules stipulate that clubs must field the strongest team available.','the rule prohibits/forbids something The rule forbids women from becoming members of the club.','the rule requires (that) ... formal (= it says that people must do something ) School rules required all girls to tie back their hair.','the rule applies to somebody/something (= it concerns them ) Everyone thinks that the rule doesn’t apply to them.','play by the rules (= do what is expected and agreed ) The system works well enough — as long as everyone plays by the rules.','bend/stretch the rules (= allow someone to do something that is not normally allowed ) They bend the rules to suit themselves.','relax the rules (= make them less strict ) Britain relaxed its immigration rules.','tighten (up) the rules (= make them stricter ) The EU has tightened the rules on the quality of drinking water.','enforce a rule (= make sure that it is obeyed ) The planning office does not always enforce its own rules.','flout a rule (= break it, without trying to hide what you are doing ) The party continues to flout its own rules.','be bound by rules (= have to obey them ) Solicitors are bound by strict rules that regulate their professional conduct.','strict They have very strict rules about gambling.','simple The rules of the game are quite simple.','petty (= unreasonable rules about unimportant things ) There are hundreds of petty rules.','a school/prison/club etc rule He had broken one of the school rules.','an unwritten rule (= a rule of behaviour that everyone in a group understands ) There’s an unwritten rule that you never call an actor before 10 a.m.','health and safety rules You should follow any health and safety rules which apply to your workplace.','be against the rules (= not be allowed ) It was against the rules to talk in class.','the rules concerning/governing/relating to something formal (= the rules about something ) the rules governing food labeling','a change in the rules I didn’t realise that there had been a change in the rules.','a breach of the rules formal (= something that is against the rules ) a serious breach of the rules','rules and regulations The government keeps introducing more and more rules and regulations.','rules are rules spoken (= a rule must be obeyed ) Rules are rules and you have to abide by them.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"As a general rule most students finish their coursework by the end of May.","translation":"به عنوان یک قاعده کلی، اکثر دانش‌آموزان دروس خود را تا پایان ماه می به پایان می‌رسانند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001774777.mp3"},{"sentence":"Early marriage used to be the rule in that part of the world.","translation":"ازدواج زودهنگام در آن نقطه از جهان یک قانون بود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001588112.mp3"},{"sentence":"A series of payments used to be the exception rather than the rule .","translation":"یک سری از پرداخت ها به جای قاعده، استثنا بود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001588116.mp3"},{"sentence":"Unfortunately there is an exception to every rule .","translation":"متأسفانه از هر قاعده ای استثنا وجود دارد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001877528.mp3"}]'::jsonb,4),
